        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0330" n="214" xml:id="pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1071.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department requests that you kindly
                    send to the United States war vessel now stationed in Dominican waters, orders
                    to convey a commission of Dominican officials, who are to be sent by the
                    President of the Republic of Santo Domingo, to confer with Mr. Desiderio Arias
                    on the north coast of the republic. It is also requested that the commander of
                    this vessel be instructed to convey this commission back to Santo Domingo City
                    after the conference.</p>
                <p>Should Mr. Arias desire to proceed to Santo Domingo City it is also requested
                    that you authorize the commander of the vessel to accede to Mr. Arias’ wishes in
                    regard to such transportation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
